From: transentient <cliff.judge@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:40:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: service the sink's IRQ_HPD over USB-C and put the sink in D3 across a DRM-initiated off

Even when USB-PD stays alive across a docked sleep (1093), resuming link
training hit AUX timeouts, and holding the DP link down for 3 minutes
without sleeping (DRM connector force off, USB host alive, altmode entered)
did the same: the dock sent IRQ_HPD Attention VDMs every 10 s, bounced HPD
after ~30 s, and its EDID could no longer be read. The sink was never told
to power down (no DP_SET_POWER D3 on a DRM-initiated off) and its IRQ_HPD
over USB-C was never serviced.

Fix both to match the downstream msm-4.19 dp_display driver:

1. Over USB-C the sink's IRQ_HPD arrives as a DisplayPort Attention VDM
   with HPD still high. typec_displayport forwards that to DRM as
   connector_status_connected, where msm_dp_aux_is_link_connected() reads 0
   because the hardware HPD pin is unused over USB-C. Route a repeat
   connected notification while dp->plugged and power_on to
   msm_dp_irq_hpd_handle() so the sink status is read and link maintenance
   runs when DP_LINK_STATUS_UPDATED is set.

2. When DRM turns the output off with the sink still attached (system
   suspend, DPMS off), msm_dp_display_disable() shuts down the mainlink and
   PHY without writing DP_SET_POWER. Put the sink in D3 first
   (msm_dp_link_psm_config(..., true)) in msm_dp_bridge_atomic_post_disable()
   when plugged and power_on, and wake it back to D0
   (msm_dp_link_psm_config(..., false)) in msm_dp_bridge_atomic_enable()
   before forced link training.

Signed-off-by: transentient <cliff.judge@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -1385,6 +1385,10 @@ void msm_dp_bridge_atomic_enable(struct drm_bridge *drm_bridge,
 
 	if (!dp->power_on) {
 		msm_dp_display_host_phy_init(msm_dp_display);
+		/* the sink was put in D3 by atomic_post_disable: wake it before training */
+		if (!dp->is_edp)
+			msm_dp_link_psm_config(msm_dp_display->link,
+					       &msm_dp_display->panel->link_info, false);
 		force_link_train = true;
 	}
 
@@ -1443,6 +1447,18 @@ void msm_dp_bridge_atomic_post_disable(struct drm_bridge *drm_bridge,
 
 	if (dp->is_edp)
 		msm_dp_hpd_unplug_handle(msm_dp_display);
+	/*
+	 * When the sink is still attached and DRM is turning the output off
+	 * (system suspend, DPMS off), put the sink in D3 while the link is
+	 * still up, as the downstream driver does in dp_display_unprepare(),
+	 * so it does not spend the sleep requesting a retrain over PD.
+	 * msm_dp_display_disable() does this on its own only when the dongle
+	 * lost its monitor (sink_count == 0).
+	 */
+	else if (dp->power_on && msm_dp_display->plugged &&
+		 msm_dp_display->link->sink_count)
+		msm_dp_link_psm_config(msm_dp_display->link,
+				       &msm_dp_display->panel->link_info, true);
 
 	msm_dp_display_disable(msm_dp_display);
 
@@ -1548,7 +1564,16 @@ void msm_dp_bridge_hpd_notify(struct drm_bridge *bridge,
 		if (hpd_link_status == ISR_HPD_REPLUG_COUNT) {
 			msm_dp_hpd_unplug_handle(dp);
 			msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(dp);
-		} else if (hpd_link_status == ISR_IRQ_HPD_PULSE_COUNT) {
+		/*
+		 * Over USB-C the sink's IRQ_HPD arrives as a DisplayPort
+		 * Attention VDM with HPD still high; the altmode driver
+		 * reports it as another "connected" while the hardware HPD
+		 * pin status is 0. Service it like the HPD-pin path does when
+		 * the link is already up: read the sink's status and retrain
+		 * if it asks for it.
+		 */
+		} else if (hpd_link_status == ISR_IRQ_HPD_PULSE_COUNT ||
+			   (dp->plugged && msm_dp_display->power_on)) {
 			msm_dp_irq_hpd_handle(dp);
 		} else {
 			msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(dp);
-- 
2.47.0
